  "details": "To go into slightly more detail, turning off fbt, or having it auto-dissable when trackers turn off (new to one of the recent versions, and what is causing issues for me personally) will offset the resting position for the controllers when they also get turned off to be somewhere infront of the user, instead of against there sides, can be re-fixed by turning fbt back on\n\nBut as someone who sleeps in vr, this is a minor problem, and wasn't a problem till the game would auto-switch to non-fbt mode when trackers turned off, instead of remaining in fbt mode with 0 trackers",
